    "body": "readStream() had no bounds check on the VInt shift count or the accumulated size value before calling QByteArray::resize(), allowing a crafted settings file to trigger an unbounded allocation (up to 2GB) and immediate OOM crash. The signed left-shift also produced undefined behavior when the shift exceeded 28 bits. Add the same overflow guard used by dataToVInt() (num2 > sizeof(int) * CHAR_BIT), stream error status checks, and a post-loop validity check on the decoded size before allocation.\r\n\r\nResolves #706\n\n<!-- Reviewable:start -->\n- - -\nThis change is [<img src=\"https://reviewable.io/review_button.svg\" height=\"34\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"Reviewable\"/>](https://reviewable.io/reviews/TokTok/qTox/707)\n<!-- Reviewable:end -->\n",
