                },
                "message": "fix: Fix OOM crash in SettingsSerializer readStream() VInt decoder.\n\nreadStream() had no bounds check on the VInt shift count or the accumulated size value before calling QByteArray::resize(), allowing a crafted settings file to trigger an unbounded allocation (up to 2GB) and immediate OOM crash. The signed left-shift also produced undefined behavior when the shift exceeded 28 bits. Add the same overflow guard used by dataToVInt() (num2 > sizeof(int) * CHAR_BIT), stream error status checks, and a post-loop validity check on the decoded size before allocation.",
